course: dictionary
lesson: 14523
title: Words that come back again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Periodically means happening again and again, from time to time, but not all the time. «The nurse checks the baby's heartbeat periodically.» The nurse does not stay and check every second. She comes back again and again, at intervals.
explain: Look inside the word. A period is a length of time that repeats, like a week or a year. So periodically can also mean happening at regular times. «The bins are emptied periodically, every Monday.» The word Monday is the clue that the timing is set.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The bins are emptied from time to time, every Monday» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Periodically means happening again and again, from time to time.
fact: It can also mean happening at regular times, like every week or every year.
fact: Periodically is an adverb: it tells you how often something happens.
fact: Phrases to remember: «checked periodically» and «update periodically».
fact: Smoke alarms should be tested periodically, so we know they still work.
exercise: «The fire alarm is tested periodically to make sure it works.» What does periodically mean? | Only once, on the day it was fitted | Very loudly | Never | *Again and again, from time to time
exercise: «The Moon goes through its phases periodically.» Which idea in this sentence shows that something repeats? | It is very bright at night | It stops suddenly and never starts again | *It goes through its phases again and again | It moves faster than a car
exercise: Mia says periodically means «all the time, without stopping». Is she right? | *No, it means from time to time, with breaks in between | Yes, it means only once | No, it means very slowly | Yes, it means the same as always
test: «The school nurse checks our height periodically.» What does this suggest? | The nurse never checks at all | The nurse checks only once in our whole lives | The nurse checks every second without a break | *The nurse checks at intervals, not all the time
test: The app will ___ so you always have the newest version. Which phrase fits best? | *update periodically | stop for ever | forget its name | glow in the dark
exam: Which word means the same as periodically? | Very quietly | Never | Suddenly and sharply | *From time to time
